# 15. COMPLETE FUNCTION REFERENCE

## 15.1 Motion Control Functions

### MotionModule Switching

```python
MotionMode(mode)          # Set module: "walk"/"action"/"head"
Motion_InitWalking()      # Switch ke walking module + delay 0.5s
Motion_InitAction()       # Switch ke action module + delay 0.5s
Motion_InitHead()         # Switch ke head module + delay 0.3s
```

### Motion Command

```python
MotionCommand(cmd)        # "start"/"stop"/"reset"
Motion_InitPose()         # Reset to initial pose (4s delay)
Motion_Start()            # Start walking engine
Motion_Stop()             # Stop walking engine + delay 0.5s
```

### Walking

```python
walking(x, y, o, t)       # Set walking params:
                          #   x: forward amplitude (±0.020)
                          #   y: side amplitude (±0.015)
                          #   o: rotation amplitude (±15)
                          #   t: period time (0.63 normal / 0.45 after kick)
```

### Action

```python
Motion_ActionNum(num)     # Execute action page (delay 3-4s)
Motion_Kick(num)          # Stop → InitAction → ActionNum → InitWalking
```

### Head Control

```python
Motion_HeadControl(pan, tilt)  # Set head position (radians)
Motion_HeadScan(enable)        # Enable/disable auto head scan
```

### LED & Buzzer

```python
LED_RGB(r, g, b)          # Set RGB LED (0-31 per channel)
LED_Status(r, g, b)       # Set status LED (0-1 per channel)
Buzzer(freq)              # Set buzzer frequency
BuzzerTone(count, period) # Buzzer pattern (count × period ms)
```

## 15.2 Odometry Control

```python
OdomStart()               # Start odometry computation
OdomStop()                # Stop odometry computation
Odom_Command(command)     # Send command: "start"/"stop"
```

### Target Setting

```python
Pointposition(x, y)       # Set target position (Pose2D)
Goalposition(jersey)      # Set goal position based on jersey:
                          #   CYAN → (900, 300)
                          #   MAGENTA → (0, 300)
```

### Navigation

```python
walk_to_position(x, y, o)    # Navigate to (x,y) then rotate to heading o
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move, in_position)

walk_follow_head(pan, tilt)  # Walk following ball head tracking
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move)

walk_ball_position_to_kick(target_pan, target_tilt, heading)
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move, is_located)

walk_rotate2(heading)        # Rotate to heading while adjusting distance
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move)

walk_rotate(heading, y_move_change)  # Simple rotate
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move, is_done)

walk_rotate_goal(heading)    # Rotate to goal heading
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move)

walk_dribble(heading)        # Dribble walk (slow forward + side adjust)
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move)

walk_in_ball_area(heading)   # Walk within ball area
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move)

walk_ball_positioning_to_goal(heading)
  returns (x_move, y_move, a_move, ball_located)
```

## 15.3 Helper Functions

### Math Utilities

```python
normalize_deg(angle)       # Normalize to 0-360°
Heading_Gap(goal, yaw)    # Shortest angular distance (-180 to 180)
map_value(val, smin, smax, tmin, tmax)    # Map with clamping
map_value2(val, smin, smax, tmin, tmax)   # Map without clamping
calculate_pid(val, set_point)             # PID controller
limit_value(val, min, max)                # Clamp value
filter_value(val, coeff)                  # Low-pass filter
scale_value(val, src, trg)                # Linear scale
min_value(a, b)                           # Minimum
max_value(a, b)                           # Maximum
```

### Detection Helpers

```python
check_ball_lost(threshold)     # Returns 1 if ball lost for N frames
check_goal_lost(threshold)     # Returns 1 if goal lost for N frames
```

### Vision Control

```python
start_tracking(state)          # True=start, False=stop ball tracking
start_positioning(state)       # True=start, False=stop goal positioning
```

### Communication

```python
udp_sendmsg(msg)               # Send message via UDP
```

### Timing

```python
Ticks()                        # Current time in milliseconds
```

## 15.4 Process Helper Functions

```python
print_once(statement)          # Print only if statement changed (reduce spam)
```

